                <divLine xml:id="m-95a431dc-c9c8-46ce-bfa8-028f3644d437" facs="#m-4fe41e5d-b080-4c74-b48b-74599c2a8ba0" form="finalis" />
              </layer>
            </staff>
            <div xml:id="m-c101af96-6bb2-4880-b06c-4b651d88abbc">
              <lg xml:id="m-c7657beb-f1ef-44c5-8528-072a31ce44e7">
                <l xml:id="m-cff99a61-3c0f-4056-a035-10b8b500804b" facs="#m-b6ca0cde-7003-4e27-ae04-10a11eb2f26a" label="ambiguous">746</l><l xml:id="m-ef301edf-7904-44f2-95f0-a9deb8ad6007" facs="#m-267d31aa-762e-46ff-93ce-816e7e81f5a5" label="ambiguous">Good Friday</l><l xml:id="m-a3e6dafe-fefa-49df-9ded-4b8e07e82bd5" facs="#m-7a3be85b-c55c-4694-b9ba-c6f02ec40cf4" label="text-like">21. The celebrant and deacon then tahe off their black stoles and put on</l><l xml:id="m-c503e54a-c0bf-48fa-b675-257aa6088f86" facs="#m-43e2456c-236c-4cb2-8dc0-7fe953d277ea" label="text-like">purple vestments, viz. asole and chasuble for the celebrant, asole and</l><l xml:id="m-c99f8b4f-7549-4fac-b60f-45d9f528a536" facs="#m-cde3242b-65cc-4337-8621-fb64dd7c1b67" label="text-like">dalmatic for the deacon and a tunicle for the subdeacon.</l><l xml:id="m-67c5d2ec-87ac-4269-be4b-0c17e97c9b0d" facs="#m-6d4f7948-dbd7-4615-a8ea-e02da1e13a8a" label="text-like">22. Then the deacon brings the burse to the altar and unfolds the corporal</l><l xml:id="m-85342e6e-5610-4dd6-a43f-f854c4c860d7" facs="#m-12fd4146-e052-4a93-8016-1b06463e4132" label="text-like">in the usual wav. An acolvie lor serverl places on the altar a small vessel ot</l><l xml:id="m-9d59c241-4d29-4178-b44d-322a7d7654cb" facs="#m-804b1802-5c99-4ea0-a79e-002b8e3510ef" label="lyrics-like">uater and a pũrificator (for ihe celebrãnt to wash and dry his fingers after</l><l xml:id="m-07ab176b-6d89-4adf-8623-87bf7a66200f" facs="#m-e3bf2e07-a338-472b-a310-bb9c3c66acdb" label="text-like">Holy Communion), and he also moves the boot to the Gospel side.</l><l xml:id="m-ca93337a-6db0-41ec-8470-357199529ac4" facs="#m-00ae54bf-3bff-4703-8cd8-f2e593bde438" label="text-like">122 a. Before the procession begins, the priest places the corporal on the</l><l xml:id="m-cdab1a0c-b969-4640-a212-5d0c1da2da40" facs="#m-fdde4ae1-36db-4ac0-924b-a580ec26aa38" label="text-like">altar and unfolds it in the usual way.]</l><l xml:id="m-a61620df-fbb6-466d-93eb-8ea4e225647f" facs="#m-9be8a0bf-ebf5-4d81-84cf-3727fd93bb05" label="text-like">23. When all is ready, the Blessed Sacrament is broughi back to the hich</l><l xml:id="m-ff5796ed-8934-42e3-89f2-09966e83bd1e" facs="#m-b2b9feea-f847-48f0-9032-c0fcd67434c9" label="text-like">altar for Holy Communion as follouos:</l><l xml:id="m-bea5e04d-9aa7-48fb-b7ad-002e1f2cd965" facs="#m-4750a861-90c5-48f1-b42e-41b780ff3360" label="text-like">The celebrant and the subdeacon, the clergy and the people all stay in their</l><l xml:id="m-d415c732-c7b3-4722-b234-f76808141fa2" facs="#m-396f8d9c-df3b-47a5-97ee-38dd2f586a0a" label="ambiguous">places in silence.</l><l xml:id="m-775b4e47-d43f-4730-ac4e-ca1fd0860515" facs="#m-185e2c46-d8db-410c-9c93-2c09a105330d" label="text-like">The deacon goes to the altar of repose with two acolytes and another cleric</l><l xml:id="m-628ad3aa-db0e-4654-8e42-b0905ac36245" facs="#m-0c7ffd77-cdf0-4a76-bb26-6ed9005b67f2" label="text-like">1o hold the ombrellino. On this altar are tuo candlestichs with lighted candles</l><l xml:id="m-dd8c6416-f5e7-406c-994f-37c8c7689b37" facs="#m-33f67cab-911a-46a7-a53b-70e844936c5e" label="text-like">in them, aohich the acolytes use for tohat follouus.</l><l xml:id="m-48b8db1b-831d-4151-b94d-2706adc21704" facs="#m-f359d2a0-42e6-44c2-b40a-099d58d82a4f" label="text-like">Al hneel at the altar of repose, and the deacon tahes the ciborium from the</l><l xml:id="m-b4ba4e96-7197-4a65-b094-37ff078814ac" facs="#m-e590d39e-3503-4ae0-94f6-e0f5796a6445" label="text-like">tabernacle. He then receives the humeral veil, covers the ciborium voith the</l><l xml:id="m-4849dcee-80b0-447f-b0f2-60ebaf0ce9ce" facs="#m-0c76a548-381d-409d-8cf2-28c9c4710c2c" label="text-like">ends of it, and brines the ciborium to the hich altar.</l><l xml:id="m-d5720f54-54eb-493b-9e1c-a395d4528db3" facs="#m-6a5bf602-acc2-4396-acc3-d6d336cd1ff2" label="text-like">(23 a. Everything is done by the celebrant woith the servers.]</l><l xml:id="m-6936493d-30d1-4249-8a57-830a0dfbc120" facs="#m-235bf2a4-a90a-475b-b6c9-0ad1846f6c4a" label="text-like">24. They come back there in the same order as they went: the ombrellino</l><l xml:id="m-aad26bf0-bc7f-4eba-a363-f202507f4dbd" facs="#m-230e41f7-0fb0-4e32-af62-173e34d14d28" label="text-like">is carried over the Blessed Sacrament, the acolytes carry lighied candles on</l><l xml:id="m-6f097bd9-cf34-44c4-858a-91255e7f828b" facs="#m-9c3b1104-8e1f-4d3e-b745-da8752892183" label="text-like">each side: evervone else kneels. Meanuhile the schola sings the follouine</l><l xml:id="m-5e5eeb00-b7f6-444d-a54f-9f01d4fd7ff5" facs="#m-db9851d2-7366-4a2c-9bf3-ee8f964ffb09" label="ambiguous">antiphons:</l><l xml:id="m-dcfad4be-1a39-4fb0-84b8-529fcba0df69" facs="#m-dcf89f8f-5b09-4a89-87e6-38b8be18bb2f" label="ambiguous">1 Ant.4</l><l xml:id="m-cea56858-08a7-4b4f-bf78-8ce8f13c45a8" facs="#m-9ea56c5c-6a0c-4d1f-9604-1e09ac3bbff4" label="lyrics-like">-do-rámus te,"Chrí-ste,</l><l xml:id="m-b21d70c8-b69f-4c30-a542-8ec37c521c70" facs="#m-9c2029db-3a99-439f-a29f-f26294d60a8d" label="ambiguous">et benedi-cimus ti-bi,</l><l xml:id="m-2d58d51d-5e41-4dde-bc17-5bf2971a1a3e" facs="#m-ca577e60-9ee1-44b9-9bd0-b506e12ca560" label="lyrics-like">qui-a per Crúcem tú-am redemísti múndum.</l><l xml:id="m-ec07c598-409c-4e2d-a434-eafdae137b5b" facs="#m-7056e463-a986-46bd-9c6f-cf9b05ea469a" label="ambiguous">2 Ant.</l><l xml:id="m-d8250ddd-017e-470c-a569-d8e4bf3cf2e2" facs="#m-0a209457-6dec-4f87-8bf6-fd8ed1620bd4" label="lyrics-like">et per sánctam</l><l xml:id="m-14179a68-32bc-453f-9d27-6d0841bd44c3" facs="#m-4b7a54a0-ce7c-450e-9f94-843784411b43" label="lyrics-like"> ER lígnum“ sérvi fá-cti sú-mus,</l><l xml:id="m-36f36a3e-c05a-4829-9f85-c7ccf07668cc" facs="#m-1e8cec17-583f-4d88-b5e3-d129ce458c75" label="lyrics-like">Crúcem libe-rá¬ ti sú-mus: frúctus ár-bo-ris sedú-xit nos,</l><l xml:id="m-0a09d1e5-6c27-4ed6-85c4-c95a72437ad2" facs="#m-838923f7-8a3d-4893-a7ca-ee0a239fbb54" label="lyrics-like">Fi-li-us Dé-i red¬</l><l xml:id="m-09d8e8ac-f009-48c8-81fc-c7d7298cf9cb" facs="#m-f9e0cad7-540a-435f-a429-cc01b8a2d5d8" label="lyrics-like">émit nos.</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
        </score>
      </mdiv>
    </body>
  </music>
</mei>